  "notes": "{群|む}れる is an intransitive ichidan verb meaning to flock, swarm, or crowd together.\n\nTRANSITIVITY:\n- Type: {自動詞|じどうし} (intransitive)\n- No transitive pair\n\nASPECT (ている):\n{群|む}れている describes the ongoing state of being gathered together: {鳥|とり}が{群|む}れている (the birds are flocking together).\n\nCOMMON PATTERNS:\n- {群|む}れをなす: to form a group/flock\n- {群|む}れてくる: to come swarming over\n- {群|む}れるのが{嫌|きら}い: to dislike running with the crowd\n\nUSAGE:\nWhen used about people, {群|む}れる can carry a negative connotation of mindlessly clustering or lacking individuality.\n\nWATCH OUT:\nDo not confuse with {蒸|む}れる (to become stuffy/humid).\n\nRELATED WORDS:\n- {群|む}れ (noun): a group, flock, herd, swarm\n- {群|むら}がる: to swarm, to crowd around (similar meaning, slightly more active)",
